<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al Jazeera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1996</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al Jazeera is a television network based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doha">Doha</a>, launched in November 1996 with funding from the emir of Qatar, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamad-bin-khalifa-al-thani">Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani</a>. As the first major Arabic news channel independent of other Arab governments it transformed the region's media, broadcasting interviews and debates rarely seen before, and won a wide audience during the wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. It added an English-language channel in 2006.</p></div>
